## 1. Result Up Front

The Block-206 H1 source passes the action-factorization test. Its apparent
matter/geometry radius-three stencil is exactly the result of multiplying
three native shifted factors. The two independent runners reconstruct every
one of the 110 literal forward Laurent terms and every one of the 110
actual-reverse terms. No single primitive shifted factor reaches beyond one
unit in either its matter or geometry variable.

This removes one important pressure for an axiom or realization change:
effective radius three does not, by itself, require a radius-three
Admissibility condition. A staged nearest-neighbor algebraic realization is
present.

The same result also locates the remaining bridge more sharply. The H1
off-diagonal shear is supplied before those factors are formed. The exact map
from all three T2 shear coordinates into the Laurent source has rank three.
The action therefore preserves every allowed shear coordinate; it does not
choose which shear actual neighboring M2 conditions should produce.

Proper-cubic covariance does not remove that choice. The conditional linear
Hom space from six Bloch-vector neighbors to the T2 shear remains exactly
two-dimensional, with the odd-shell and even-shell maps of Block 206.

Finally, the strongest simple shortcut fails as a uniqueness argument. If the
six alternative source phases are overgenerously promoted to six simultaneous
equatorial Bloch contents, eight of the 24 possible internal proper-cubic
frames can be paired with odd/even coefficients to reproduce the one H1
shear. The eight resulting law maps are distinct, and every one of their 28
pairs disagrees on a held-out one-site basis condition.

That comparator is not a physical negative theorem because the six phases are
alternative experiments, not an inherited six-record state. It proves only
that the visible H1 phase pattern cannot be used to claim unique decoder
selection.

