## 3. Exact Native Factorization

For each relevant spatial index mu, the native centered cosine is a two-term
Laurent factor C_mu. For incoming and outgoing centered differences write
d_in and d_out. Every monomial of C_mu and d_in shifts its matter coordinate
by one unit at most; every monomial of C_mu and d_out shifts both its matter
and geometry coordinates by one unit at most.

For the two nonzero off-diagonal H1 slots, the Hodge vertex and action vertex
are

~~~
H_mu_nu =
  -(C_mu C_nu)/sqrt(2)
   (c_mu a_nu + c_nu a_mu),

V_mu_nu =
  m H_mu_nu
  + i H_mu_nu d_in
  + i d_out^T H_mu_nu.
~~~

The runner constructs each product in that order and combines slots 02 and 12
only after their native paths are complete. The exact stage census is:

| stage | Laurent terms | max matter L1 | max geometry L1 |
|---|---:|---:|---:|
| two-cosine product | 8 | 2 | 2 |
| local Hodge multiplication | 8 | 2 | 2 |
| mass piece | 8 | 2 | 2 |
| incoming-difference piece | 60 | 3 | 2 |
| outgoing-difference piece | 60 | 3 | 3 |
| combined H1 source | 110 | 3 | 3 |

The maximum shifted-factor depth is three. Direct expansion equals the
inherited Block-206 source exactly. Applying the actual reverse exponent map
independently to the staged and inherited sources again gives exact equality
with 110 terms.

This is an algebraic factor-locality theorem. The factors act on the
four-dimensional exterior carrier used by the candidate action. No runner in
this campaign turns them into a legal sequence of one-site M2 instruments or
Record writes.

## 4. Why Factorization Does Not Select The Decoder

Let S map the three T2 shear coordinates to the full Laurent source by the
native action formula. The runner flattens every exact Laurent coefficient
matrix, not just a convenient momentum evaluation, and obtains

~~~
rank(S)=3.
~~~

Thus no shear coordinate is erased by the action. For any conditional decoder

~~~
D_(a,b) = a D_odd + b D_even,
~~~

the native construction simply forms S composed with D_(a,b). Factor order,
mass versus difference pieces, literal-forward consistency, and
actual-reverse consistency all apply after the output of D_(a,b) has been
chosen. They produce no equation fixing a or b.

This statement is deliberately narrow:

> In the frozen H1 construction, the native action factorization,
> whose input is an already-supplied TT shear, does not itself select a
> physical eta-to-shear decoder.

It is not the broader statement that no local, nonlinear, compiler-derived,
or differently encoded decoder can exist.

